// RSA right and flat-rate amount (L.262-2/3/4/5, R.262-1/2/39).
//
// DEONTIC MAP: computation only (no must/must-not here):
// - the L.262-2 euro base of a single person is BUILT from the pinned
//   revaluation decrees 2020-490, 2021-530, 2022-699, 2023-340, 2024-396 and
//   2025-293 (article 1; bareme parameter MontantForfaitaireDecret, read at
//   the legal time of the case; DECISION-0452: the amount is constructed, not
//   substituted). The window 2022-07-01..2023-03-31 belongs to law 2022-1158
//   art. 9 (coefficient 1.04 on every amount revalued under L. 161-25, which
//   L. 262-3 al. 1 says of the montant forfaitaire): there the base is BUILT
//   as the amount of decree 2022-699 x 1.04 rounded to the centime HALF_UP
//   (rule MfBaseLoi2022). The rounding is not in the text of art. 9, of
//   L. 161-25 or of L. 262-3, so it is a READING (SPEC 152, owner decision
//   08.10.2026, basis: practice of the funds): interpretation
//   MfJuillet2022ArrondiCentime, selected in the context of the case; unselected
//   the window stays without a built base. Outside the pinned series (from
//   2026-04-01, the next 1 April, not pinned) the base stays a case input
//   (mf_base; B-RSA-MF-EURO, DSS_PENDING), and a supplied mf_base wins over
//   the decree (the fund-retained base of the case);
// - the household flat-rate follows from that base and the composition by
//   R.262-1 (rank scale below); the MF of the right month (increase included,
//   mf_applicable_mois) is carried to the three months of the reference
//   quarter as fr.minima.ressources::mf_mois, and the size-class amounts as
//   fr.minima.ressources::mf_composition (B-RSA-MF-INPUT-CONTRACT closed from
//   this side: a case no longer supplies them);
// - the quarterly amount DUE arrives from fr.minima.ressources
//   (montant_du_trimestre = average of the monthly intermediate amounts,
//   R.262-7 I, same lane) and is consumed AS the due: droit holds when
//   the due is positive (due > 0 stands for resources < MF, L.262-2
//   al.1) and the allowance EQUALS the due (L.262-2 al.2); never
//   subtract it from the MF again (D-26, D-44: the W4 consumer-side
//   double subtraction, repaired here);
// - L.262-6 EU specifics and the L.262-4 2° exemption list arrive inside
//   sejour_travail_condition (fund-established, README);
// - in a household made of one or two parents and their dependent children,
//   ranks 5+ are built from the counted persons; no rate-class input is needed.
// The 50/30/40 person-rank scale follows the pinned R.262-1 (+50 % for the
// second person, +30 % for each further dependant, +40 % from the third
// child or under-25 dependant); the foreign reference (OpenFisca rsa_socle)
// only corroborates it.

